@startuml
title PackageSubscription - paid coverage lifecycle (REVIEW)
[*] --> NotPurchased
NotPurchased --> ACTIVE : first fee + cycle committed
ACTIVE --> ACTIVE : explicit extension / version matches\none fee, extend coverageEnd
ACTIVE --> PENDING_CANCEL : durable cancellation accepted\nfreeze cancelEffectiveAt=coverageEnd
PENDING_CANCEL --> CANCELLED : now >= cancelEffectiveAt\nno refund, preserve all paid cycles
ACTIVE --> EXPIRED : now >= coverageEnd\nno successful renewal / insufficient MAIN
EXPIRED --> ACTIVE : explicit re-registration\nor eligible delayed renewal\none new cycle starts now
ACTIVE --> ACTIVE : one valid renewal committed\nno retroactive coverage
CANCELLED --> ACTIVE : explicit later purchase if policy permits\nnew paid cycle, never undo cancellation
note right of ACTIVE
 State alone does not grant rights.
 A committed cycle must cover checkedAt in [start,end).
 API denies at expiry even before daily job updates state.
 expectedVersion + shared cycle guard prevents duplicate fees.
end note
note right of PENDING_CANCEL
 No extensions / automatic renewal.
 Existing prepaid future cycles remain usable.
 Current-cycle end is not necessarily coverageEnd.
end note
note bottom of EXPIRED
 FAILED insufficient-funds attempt is final.
 No automatic resurrection after credit.
 Delayed technical recovery follows Q25, not retry of business FAILED.
end note
@enduml
